<script>
	import Callout from '$lib/components/Callout.svelte';
</script>

Networks and rate limiters fail in predictable, retryable ways. ApiTool's retry logic
targets exactly those — transient 5xx, 429 throttling, connection resets, timeouts —
while letting you fence off the requests that must *never* be retried. Pair it with a
collection-wide rate limit and your suite stops being flaky.

## The collection

```yaml
# collections/resilient.yaml
name: Resilient calls
rate_limit_rps: 10                  # token bucket across the whole collection

requests:
  - name: Fetch report
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "{{base_url}}/reports/{{report_id}}"
    retry:
      enabled: true
      max_attempts: 5               # 1 initial + 4 retries
      initial_delay_ms: 500
      max_delay_ms: 30000
      backoff_strategy: exponential # exponential | linear | constant
      jitter: true
      jitter_factor: 0.2            # spread retries to avoid thundering herds
      respect_retry_after: true     # honor the server's Retry-After header
      retry_on:
        status_codes: [429, 502, 503, 504]
        status_ranges: ["5xx"]
        network_errors: true        # connection refused, DNS failure, reset
        timeouts: true
      do_not_retry_on:
        status_codes: [401, 403]    # config errors — retrying won't help
    assertions:
      status: 200
      timing:
        max_duration_ms: 10000
```

## The delay sequence

With `exponential`, `initial_delay_ms: 500`, capped at `30000`:

| Retry | Delay (no jitter) |
|---|---|
| 1 | 500 ms |
| 2 | 1000 ms |
| 3 | 2000 ms |
| 4 | 4000 ms |

Jitter at `0.2` multiplies each delay by `1 + 0.2 × random(-1, 1)`, so retry 3 lands
anywhere in `[1600, 2400]` ms. When the server sends `Retry-After`, that value wins
(up to a 30s cap).

## Run it

```bash
apitest run collections/resilient.yaml --var report_id=R-2026-001
```

```
Collection: Resilient calls
  ✓ Fetch report  200  1844ms

────────────────────────────────
  1 request(s): 1 passed, 0 failed (1844ms)
```

<Callout type="output">
	Representative output — the request needed two retries (503 → 503 → 200), absorbed
	silently before the assertions ran. Add <code>-v</code> to see each attempt and its
	computed backoff delay.
</Callout>

<Callout type="warn">
	<code>POST</code> and <code>PATCH</code> aren't idempotent — retrying one that
	already succeeded server-side can create duplicates. ApiTool warns when you enable
	retry for non-idempotent methods. Restrict it with <code>retry_on.methods</code>,
	add the verb to <code>do_not_retry_on.methods</code>, or send an idempotency key
	(as the <a href="/examples/checkout-flow">checkout flow</a> does).
</Callout>
